I do this all the time, emailing savefiles back and forth from work to
home and vice versa.  Both computers run 3.4.3 unpatched on win32.

The work computer names files in the following manner:

firstname.lastname-charname.nethack-saved-game

The home computer names files as:

firstname-charname.nethack-saved-game

Simply renaming the files allows them to be transferred between the
two machines.  I usually play lots of characters at work (nethack
makes conference calls go quicker) and only email promising ones to
the home computer where I can play them with more time to concentrate
on them.

